          "question": "What blood pressure target does guidance describe for most adults?",
          "answer": "For most adults, clinical guidance suggests a blood pressure target below 130/80 mm Hg. This target is mentioned in the Major Cardiology Society consensus guidance on Coronary Artery Disease: Secondary Prevention (guideline-coronary-artery-disease-secondary-prevention).\n\nThe guidance notes that specific conditions can influence the choice of blood pressure medication, but the target itself remains consistent for most.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
